+# finder-kde
+
+**Finder for KDE Plasma**: KDE's [Dolphin](https://apps.kde.org/dolphin/)
+file manager rebuilt to look and work like the macOS (Golden Gate) Finder.
+It installs as a separate app called Finder, next to stock Dolphin, with its
+own settings.
+
+Based on Dolphin 26.08.1. Every Finder change is a commit on top of the
+`v26.08.1` tag, and the upstream code is marked `Finder:` where it was changed.
+
+## What's different from Dolphin
+
+- **Window**: frameless, rounded, with its own stoplights (close, minimize,
+  zoom), a native shadow, and a translucent glass sidebar that runs to the
+  top of the window. Drag empty toolbar space to move; double-click to zoom.
+- **Toolbar**: glass capsules for back/forward, the view modes (icons, list,
+  columns), Group By, a "…" actions menu and search. The folder name is
+  shown as a bold title; click it (or Ctrl+L) to type a path.
+- **Sidebar**: Recents, Favorites and Locations, with accent-tinted icons,
+  rounded selection, mount-on-click for drives, and AirDrop.
+- **Icon view**: Finder's selection (a gray tile behind the icon and a blue
+  pill behind the name), no hover or focus boxes.
+- **List view**: Name / Date Modified / Size / Kind columns, flat header
+  with the sort column in bold, zebra stripes that fill the view, full-row
+  blue selection, disclosure chevrons, "Today at 4:49 PM" dates and decimal
+  sizes ("245 KB", "--" for folders).
+- **Column view** (new): Miller columns with a preview column, its own
+  context menu, and a title and footer that follow the active column.
+- **Footer**: "16 items, 727 GB available" / "1 of 16 selected", with the
+  zoom slider.
+- **AirDrop** with iPhones and Macs: AirDrop in the sidebar (Ctrl+Shift+R),
+  right-click › Share › AirDrop, progress cards for sending and receiving,
+  and notifications. See below.
+
+## Install
+
+```sh
+finder-extras/install.sh --deps   # first time: build dependencies (Fedora)
+finder-extras/install.sh          # build and install into ~/.local/opt/finder
+```
+
+Finder then shows up in your app menu. To make it the default file manager:
+
+```sh
+xdg-mime default org.brhett.finder.desktop inode/directory
+```
+
+## AirDrop
+
+AirDrop runs on [omdrop-owl](https://github.com/t4t5/omdrop-owl), the open
+AirDrop radio for non-Apple Wi-Fi cards, and
+[omdrop](https://github.com/netmojo-systems/omdrop-plugin). On Fedora,
+`finder-extras/install-airdrop` builds and installs both and opens the
+AirDrop port in firewalld.
+
+It depends on your Wi-Fi card (see omdrop-owl's hardware table). On most
+Intel cards AirDrop takes the card over, so **Wi-Fi disconnects while
+AirDrop is on** and reconnects afterwards. Finder warns before turning it on.
+
+## Upstream
+
+Dolphin is © the KDE community, and Finder keeps its license
+(GPL-2.0-or-later; see [COPYING](COPYING) and [LICENSES](LICENSES)). The
+original README is in [README.dolphin.md](README.dolphin.md). Finder is not
+affiliated with KDE or Apple.
diff --git a/finder-extras/install-airdrop b/finder-extras/install-airdrop
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..cc81909f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/finder-extras/install-airdrop
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Set up AirDrop for Finder: omdrop-owl (the AirDrop radio for non-Apple
+# Wi-Fi cards, github.com/t4t5/omdrop-owl) and omdrop (the send/receive
+# tool, github.com/netmojo-systems/omdrop-plugin), plus a narrow firewall
+# opening. Finder's AirDrop sidebar item, Share › AirDrop menu and
+# progress cards all run on these.
+#
+#   install-airdrop      build and install (asks for your password through
+#                        the system prompt for the root steps)
+#
+# Fedora (dnf + firewalld) is what this was written and tested on; on other
+# distributions follow the two projects' READMEs instead.
+#
+# Heads-up: on most Intel Wi-Fi cards AirDrop takes the card over, so Wi-Fi
+# disconnects while AirDrop is on and reconnects when it turns off.
+set -euo pipefail
+
+src=${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/mac-glass-kde/airdrop-src
+
+command -v dnf >/dev/null || { echo "install-airdrop handles Fedora (dnf) only; see the omdrop-owl README for other systems." >&2; exit 1; }
+
+echo "Installing build tools…"
+pkexec dnf -y install rpm-build cmake gcc gcc-c++ make git libev-devel libpcap-devel libnl3-devel keyutils python3-libarchive-c
+
+mkdir -p "$src"
+for repo in t4t5/omdrop-owl netmojo-systems/omdrop-plugin; do
+    dir=$src/$(basename "$repo")
+    if [ -d "$dir/.git" ]; then
+        git -C "$dir" pull -q --ff-only
+    else
+        git clone -q --depth 1 "https://github.com/$repo.git" "$dir"
+    fi
+done
+
+echo "Building the AirDrop radio (omdrop-owl)…"
+(cd "$src/omdrop-owl" && rm -f omdrop-owl-*.rpm && tools/build-rpm.sh)
+rpm=$(ls "$src"/omdrop-owl/omdrop-owl-*.rpm | head -n1)
+# pkexec runs in root's home, so the package needs its full path.
+pkexec dnf -y install "$rpm"
+
+echo "Setting up omdrop…"
+"$src/omdrop-plugin/bin/omdrop" setup
+
+# The receiver listens on TCP 8771 (and answers discovery on UDP 5353) on
+# the AirDrop interface only; open exactly that, to link-local peers.
+if systemctl is-active -q firewalld; then
+    echo "Opening the AirDrop port in firewalld…"
+    pkexec sh -c '
+        firewall-cmd -q --permanent --get-zones | tr " " "\n" | grep -qx airdrop || firewall-cmd -q --permanent --new-zone=airdrop
+        firewall-cmd -q --permanent --zone=airdrop --add-interface=awdl0 || true
+        firewall-cmd -q --permanent --zone=airdrop --add-rich-rule="rule family=ipv6 source address=fe80::/10 port port=8771 protocol=tcp accept"
+        firewall-cmd -q --permanent --zone=airdrop --add-rich-rule="rule family=ipv6 source address=fe80::/10 port port=5353 protocol=udp accept"
+        firewall-cmd -q --reload'
+elif command -v ufw >/dev/null; then
+    "$HOME/.local/bin/omdrop" firewall install
+fi
+
+"$HOME/.local/bin/omdrop" doctor
+echo "AirDrop is set up. In Finder: AirDrop in the sidebar (Ctrl+Shift+R), or right-click a file › Share › AirDrop."
diff --git a/finder-extras/install.sh b/finder-extras/install.sh
new file mode 100755
index 000000000..11a0f78e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/finder-extras/install.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Build Finder from this checkout and install it for the current user, into
+# ~/.local/opt/finder with a launcher entry. Stock Dolphin is untouched:
+# Finder is a separate app with its own settings (finderrc).
+#
+#   finder-extras/install.sh           build and install
+#   finder-extras/install.sh --deps    first install Dolphin's build
+#                                      dependencies (Fedora; asks for your password)
+set -euo pipefail
+
+root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
+prefix=$HOME/.local/opt/finder
+apps=${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/applications
+
+if [ "${1:-}" = --deps ]; then
+    pkexec dnf -y builddep dolphin
+fi
+
+for tool in cmake ninja g++; do
+    command -v "$tool" >/dev/null || { echo "missing $tool (try: $0 --deps)" >&2; exit 1; }
+done
+
+cmake -S "$root" -B "$root/build" -G Ninja \
+    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$prefix" \
+    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_RPATH="$prefix/lib64" \
+    -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF
+# Half the cores: a full-width build can run a 16 GB machine out of memory.
+ninja -C "$root/build" -j"$(( $(nproc) / 2 > 0 ? $(nproc) / 2 : 1 ))"
+ninja -C "$root/build" install
+
+mkdir -p "$apps"
+sed "s|@PREFIX@|$prefix|" "$root/finder-extras/org.brhett.finder.desktop" > "$apps/org.brhett.finder.desktop"
+update-desktop-database "$apps" 2>/dev/null || true
+echo "Finder installed. Launch it from the app menu, or: $prefix/bin/finder"
+echo "For AirDrop, run finder-extras/install-airdrop."
